    {
      "id": "06ec5f2e4af2f30e91149cd96ce34ef8c7b67af3",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1737175097,
          "type": null,
          "body": "I can even imagine a somewhat useful filter macro that accepts a null argument, something that has `protocol$1` where if $1 is null it matches the entire protocol but otherwise something like `.field` is entered. But I don't see how else to make the new filter macro grammar work with zero arguments, especially since $field is now allowed for field references (and could match just a protocol.)",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-01-22T22:50:02.345Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-01-22T22:50:02.345Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 276521310,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 14124,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "af253c02079dd2cb56c6d01a3a641c8e2efbd958",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1738403399,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Macros that accept a null argument are I think a subset of macros for which spaces are significant. The argument parsing of macros includes spaces, and everything include the spaces are substituted in. For the typical macro definition, where the argument `$N` is surrounded by spaces, that doesn't matter, but it's possible to write clever macros where it is used.\n\nThe case of *interior* space in a macro argument is a somewhat more straightforward to understand, and possibly more useful (also allowing macros as arguments to your macros so you can macro while you macro), but still occasionally confusing.\n\n(Our documentation implies that it is ignored, which is perhaps misleading.)",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
